// Slicing a string with a negative stride fails. `a and ...` evaluates the
// right operand where `a` is null, so the whole conjunction would fail the
// pipeline. The split chain drops the event at `a` and never slices `x`, which
// the optimizer may do because the event does not pass either way.
from {a: null, x: "abc"}
where a and x.slice(stride=-1) == ""
